Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Fail NtGetContextThread on a NULL context on ARM64EC.

The ARM64EC NtGetContextThread reads context->ContextFlags before it
does anything else, so a NULL context faults at address 0x30, the
offset of ContextFlags in the AMD64 CONTEXT. Windows probes the buffer
and returns STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION, and GetThreadContext returns FALSE.

Crash Bandicoot N. Sane Trilogy calls GetThreadContext with a NULL
context from a Steam callback about seven seconds after its title
screen loads. The game dies there under ARM64EC with an unhandled page
fault in ntdll, so it never gets past the title screen.

Return STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION for a NULL context, as Windows does.
---
 dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
@@ -718,8 +718,12 @@
 
 NTSTATUS SYSCALL_API NtGetContextThread( HANDLE handle, CONTEXT *context )
 {
-    ARM64_NT_CONTEXT arm_ctx = { .ContextFlags = ctx_flags_x64_to_arm( context->ContextFlags ) };
-    NTSTATUS status = syscall_NtGetContextThread( handle, &arm_ctx );
+    ARM64_NT_CONTEXT arm_ctx;
+    NTSTATUS status;
+
+    if (!context) return STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION;
+    arm_ctx = (ARM64_NT_CONTEXT){ .ContextFlags = ctx_flags_x64_to_arm( context->ContextFlags ) };
+    status = syscall_NtGetContextThread( handle, &arm_ctx );
 
     if (!status) context_arm_to_x64( (ARM64EC_NT_CONTEXT *)context, &arm_ctx );
     return status;
